    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0150" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1133: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-09T12:00:00+03:00">July 9,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received July 9—9:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Referring to the last sentence of my telegram No. 56, June 27,<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d184-f1"/> reliable sources of information confirm the activity of
                    Italian submarines in the Indian Ocean and Persian Gulf. One was rammed recently
                    at the entrance of the Gulf by a British destroyer and another spotted in the
                    Gulf is being searched for today by British bombing planes. Steamer service
                    between Iraq and India is uncertain and fully booked for at least next 6 weeks.
                    I am encouraging Americans evacuating through here to travel when possible by
                    air to Karachi and thence by rail to Bombay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
